      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to evaluate \\(\\left\\lceil -\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}} \\right\\rceil\\).\n\nFirst, we start by finding the value inside the square root:\n\\[\n\\frac{49}{4}\n\\]\n\nNext, we compute the square root of \\(\\frac{49}{4}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}} = \\sqrt{49} \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}} = 7 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{7}{2}\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the negative of this value:\n\\[\n-\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}} = -\\frac{7}{2}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to apply the ceiling function to \\(-\\frac{7}{2}\\). The ceiling function, \\(\\left\\lceil x \\right\\rceil\\), returns the smallest integer greater than or equal to \\(x\\).\n\nThe value inside the ceiling function is \\(-\\frac{7}{2}\\), which is equivalent to \\(-3.5\\). The smallest integer greater than or equal to \\(-3.5\\) is \\(-3\\).\n\nThus, we have:\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil -\\frac{7}{2} \\right\\rceil = \\left\\lceil -3.5 \\right\\rceil = -3\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-3}\n\\]",
